diagnostics/lambda-loop-exits.em:1:17: `break` can only be used inside a loop
  [1].each { x => break }
                  ^^^^^
`break` ends a `for` or `while` loop; a block passed to `each` or `map` is not a loop. Write a `for` loop over the items instead, as in `for item in items`.
diagnostics/lambda-loop-exits.em:2:17: `continue` can only be used inside a loop
  [1].each { x => continue }
                  ^^^^^^^^
`continue` moves to the next turn of a `for` or `while` loop; a block is not a loop. To skip an item, `return` from the block.
diagnostics/lambda-loop-exits.em:4:21: `break` can only be used inside a loop
      [1].each { x => break if x > 0 }
                      ^^^^^
`break` ends a `for` or `while` loop; a block passed to `each` or `map` is not a loop. Write a `for` loop over the items instead, as in `for item in items`.
diagnostics/lambda-loop-exits.em:5:21: `continue` can only be used inside a loop
      [1].each { x => continue if x > 0 }
                      ^^^^^^^^
`continue` moves to the next turn of a `for` or `while` loop; a block is not a loop. To skip an item, `return` from the block.
